SUMMARY:Bearwallow Mountain Trail\nFull Moon Hike - 2.1 mi. 587' g.
DESCRIPTION:The Asheville Hiking Group\nThis Full Moon\, commonly known as
  the Buck Moon\, will have an illumination of 99.8% at a distance of 248\,
 926 miles. Current weather forecast calls for sunny skies and and a low th
 at evening around 63. Once the sun sets it may become a little chilly at 4
 \,232' elevation so consider bringing a light jacket. The ascent is around
  one mile and will take us an estimated 30 minutes but it's challenging en
 ough to elevate your heart rate. For safety purposes we will take the wide
  fire service road back to our cars.\n\nWe will gather at the Fresh Market
  on Hendersonville Rd. at 6:15 and depart at 6:30\, taking the "back way" 
 as Highway 74 is still limited to local traffic beyond Gerton. Parking can
  be tight at the trailhead so carpooling is essential.\n\nNOTE! Bring a he
 ad lamp or flashlight with a red lense "for emergency purposes" only. We d
 o not use flashlights as it will be bright enough to see our way down the 
 wide gravel road and they detract from the experience. I'll also try and r
 emember to bring some glow sticks to attach around our ankles.\nIf you hav
 e night vision problems or are unstable in low light situations this hike 
 is probably not for you.\n\nWear appropriate shoes\, bring water\, snacks\
 , and maybe a lite blanket to sit on. Poles are optional.\n\nSunset is at 
 8:36 p:m and the Moon rises at 8:55 p:m. Plan on relaxing and enjoying thi
 s celestial event with others. We will begin to head back down around 9:15
  - 9:30. I estimate getting back to our cars around 10:00 p:m.\nGuests nee
 d to join Asheville Hiking Group and sign up for this hike on their own.\n
 \nBeing how erratic our weather has been lately\, if there is a change in 
 the forecast that necessitates canceling\, I will do so by 5:00 p:m Wednes
 day. Only sign up if you truly plan to attend. If you must cancel\, do so 
 asap to allow any wait-listers ample time. No shows = not cool.\n\nAny que
 stions please feel free to message me through this Meetup app.\n\nLegal St
 uff: This Asheville Hiking Group (AHG) event involves hiking and\, possibl
 y\, transportation to and from the meetup site. Participants are responsib
 le for their own safety and affirm that they have the appropriate skills\,
  physical conditioning\, equipment\,and supplies. Hiking may involve risks
  to oneself and property. Neither your hike organizer nor Asheville Hiking
  Group can assure your safety nor eliminate all risks. Participants assume
  full responsibility for any injuries or losses.
